WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.501
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.032
- [Erdin] Innovation
doesn't happen on its own.

00:00:04.032 --> 00:00:06.137
It needs leaders to drive it.

00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:09.005
The Innovation Leadership Bootcamp,

00:00:09.005 --> 00:00:12.477
is not just your regular online program.

00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:15.392
It is immersive and it is intense.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.211
- [Ingrid] You're going
to interact with people

00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:20.692
from all around the world.

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:22.963
Learn from the best experts

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:24.834
and receive personalized feedback

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.225
from amazing entrepreneurs.

00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:29.276
- [Erdin] Our coaches are MIT alumni

00:00:29.276 --> 00:00:32.808
who are entrepreneurs,
executives, or investors.

00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:36.991
They understand what it takes
to generate an innovation

00:00:36.991 --> 00:00:39.682
and to design a venture to support it.

00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:42.594
- [Mariah] They're going
to be able to push you past

00:00:42.594 --> 00:00:44.465
what you thought was possible.

00:00:44.465 --> 00:00:48.127
- [Erdin] You will get wide
exposure to MIT faculty

00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:51.859
for pushing the frontiers
in different fields.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:53.730
- [Vimala] Like many MIT courses,

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.352
the Bootcamp is a living lab,

00:00:56.352 --> 00:01:00.314
where we're asking you to
identify important problems,

00:01:00.314 --> 00:01:04.389
produce your own data and
create an effective solution.

00:01:06.757 --> 00:01:07.591
- [Mariah] The Bootcamp

00:01:07.591 --> 00:01:10.800
is a team project-based
learning experience.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.471
So, you will collaborate with people

00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:15.852
from extremely diverse backgrounds.

00:01:15.852 --> 00:01:18.784
People who push you to look
at the world differently,

00:01:18.784 --> 00:01:20.945
and over the course of those 10 weeks,

00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:24.797
you will build a venture
with your team members.

00:01:24.797 --> 00:01:27.239
- [Vimala] We really embrace
real-world challenges

00:01:27.239 --> 00:01:29.350
and real big problems.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:32.171
- [Erdin] You will see ventures
targeting sustainability,

00:01:32.171 --> 00:01:34.833
education, economic inclusion.

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:37.434
It's about whether you
can design a solution

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:40.039
that is superior and sustainable.

00:01:41.016 --> 00:01:42.867
- [Vimala] It's not
just for entrepreneurs.

00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:47.470
It's really for anyone who
wants to learn how to identify

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:50.121
and solve problems effectively.

00:01:50.121 --> 00:01:52.002
- [Mariah] Really successful
Bootcampers are willing

00:01:52.002 --> 00:01:55.114
to immerse themselves in
the collaborative experience

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.265
and do so with energy.

00:01:57.265 --> 00:01:59.316
- [Vimala] Each of our cohorts has people

00:01:59.316 --> 00:02:02.698
from anywhere from 30 to
60 different countries.

00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:06.230
We really think about
selecting our future members

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.961
for this innovation community

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.582
that we're helping to build.

00:02:09.582 --> 00:02:11.393
- [Ingrid] The Bootcamp
community is this place

00:02:11.393 --> 00:02:13.975
where amazing people around the world

00:02:13.975 --> 00:02:15.616
that really want to change things,

00:02:15.616 --> 00:02:17.817
that want to grow, that are ambitious,

00:02:17.817 --> 00:02:21.082
meet other people that
are doing the same things.

00:02:22.039 --> 00:02:23.640
- [Erdin] MIT Bootcamps is not just

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.368
about meeting your potential,
it's about expanding it.

00:02:27.368 --> 00:02:30.120
(relaxing music)

